{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"99f993a06d453978ae0e372f46753510aa3c8cceea5589047eef874c9cbed970","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_03a88f39856b71e92a0e3b604d85ec3e037a6864ce3916a0431a10af62f5075f","overall_assessment":"The paper has a significant policy violation regarding anonymity (POL-ANO) due to the presence of author and affiliation details on the title page. Additionally, it lacks explicit data licensing compliance statements (POL-DAT) and broader impact discussions (POL-IMP), which are increasingly expected in modern research submissions.","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_identity_sha256":"3696103dd83e30d790044b849dadd1c37e324386b82c04b0124fa993d9a629b6","prompt_identity_sha256":"e47b344c9843ff2eafbb72038e65dde05f2c9471d8c06d8a8ea455f6bd3b6be2","raw_response_sha256":"519825c919fe216408ac0041835909f862096424a42829753f2d81d1cfbd4216","request_identity_sha256":"ffca065a3ce7e8c98596efb69e898dcd35de89e9d344623e5c607efdae8f905b","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. While the model is a standard document representation technique, there is no discussion of bias in the learned embeddings or the impact of the 'corruption' mechanism on the representation of specific demographic or linguistic groups. The lack of ethical consideration is a minor weakness for a 2017 submission, as such statements were not yet standard, but it remains a gap in responsible AI compliance.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-031","SRC-036"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes several public datasets: IMDB movie reviews, a subset of the Wikipedia dump, and the SICK dataset (SemEval 2014). The authors describe the data sources and preprocessing steps (e.g., removing words appearing less than 10 times) but do not explicitly state the licensing terms or confirm that the usage complies with the specific licenses of these datasets (e.g., Wikipedia's CC-BY-SA or SICK's research-only license). While these are standard academic datasets, explicit confirmation of license compliance is absent.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper violates double-blind review policies. The title page explicitly lists the author's name ('Minmin Chen'), institutional affiliation ('Criteo Research'), location ('Palo Alto, CA 94301, USA'), and email address ('m.chen@criteo.com'). This information is clearly visible in the provided text and would compromise the anonymity required for peer review at venues like ICLR.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission in the provided text. The paper cites relevant prior work (Word2Vec, Paragraph Vectors, etc.) appropriately. The methodology and results appear to be original contributions, with proper attribution to foundational techniques like negative sampling and dropout.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper lacks a broader impact statement or a discussion of the societal implications of the technology. It does not mention code or data availability, nor does it specify software licenses for any released artifacts. While the model is efficient, the absence of a broader impact section or checklist compliance (if required by the venue) is a weakness in terms of transparency and reproducibility standards.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"742c9b744eba61767dbb774c02147d2473e671b080b13181a84c274105a7fb5a","paper_id":"B1Igu2ogg","paper_ordinal":7,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha2